commit 729afff93aaedda81faf1d1badf44ac3bea9cd85
Author: humaux <luogangan7@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 02:01:01 2026 +0800

    ci: install only the Playwright engines each browser mode needs; bounded apt retries (#27)
    
    * ci: derive Playwright engines and bound apt dependency retries
    
    * docs(ci): deliver mode-specific Playwright deps and retry calibration
    
    * test(ci): create the untracked output/playwright parent before mkdtemp (PR #27 review)
    
    On a fresh checkout output/playwright does not exist, so five installer tests threw ENOENT and the
    foundation Node gate failed. Red (dir absent): 5 pass/5 fail; green: 10/10.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * fix(auth): resend countdown reads the clock once (WebKit showed 61 s)
    
    sendStep1 called Date.now() twice (setNow, then setResendAt). When the two reads straddled a
    millisecond, ceil((resendAt-now)/1000) rendered 'Send a new code in 61 s', so the reset
    enumeration-parity test (known vs unknown address must render identical text) failed on the
    slower WebKit engine in PR #27 CI run (password-auth step). Not an enumeration leak: the
    cooldown is a client constant for both. Test unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
